   "fieldtype": "HTML",
   "label": "Temperature Help",
   "options": "<div class=\"small\" style=\"border:1px solid var(--border-color);border-radius:6px;padding:8px 10px\"><b>How temperature recording works.</b> The system does not read the fridge by itself. Staff read the fridge&#39;s own thermometer or display and enter it here.<table class=\"table table-bordered table-sm\" style=\"margin:6px 0\"><tr><th>Storage</th><th>Keep between</th><th>Record</th></tr><tr><td>Blood fridge (Whole Blood, Red Cells)</td><td>2 and 6 \u00b0C</td><td>At least twice a day (morning and evening shift), or every 4 hours if the fridge has no alarm</td></tr><tr><td>Plasma freezer (FFP, Plasma)</td><td>-18 \u00b0C or colder</td><td>At least twice a day</td></tr><tr><td>Platelet agitator</td><td>20 and 24 \u00b0C</td><td>At least twice a day, and check it is shaking</td></tr></table>Out of range: the Blood Bank Officer is notified straight away and decides whether the bags in that storage are kept or discarded. The reading history is the proof for audits. Fridges with a Wi-Fi logger can be connected later, so readings come in automatically.</div>"
